  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 1250 PM Monday... \n\nKEY MESSAGE 1... Continued dry with moderating temperatures through \nthe week.\n\nAt the surface, a 1033 mb Canadian high over the OH Valley will \nslowly migrate eastward to the mid-Atlantic through mid-week, then \nremain in place and moderate through the end of the week. Aloft, the \npositively tilted longwave trough will shift offshore, while a s/w \nsettles over the Gulf Coast and cuts off from the trough. This will \nset up a Rex Block as the sub-tropical ridge, amplifying to the west \ntoday and Tue, shifts east. The high should progress ewd across the \ncntl Appalachians and mid-Atlantic then offshore, while the low sits \nover the Gulf Coast Tue night through Thu. Expect dry weather with \nmoderating temperatures beneath the high through at least Fri.\n\nNear to below freezing low temperatures are expected across much of \ncentral NC through mid-week, though the urban areas and portions of \nthe Sandhills and Coastal Plain may be above freezing by Thu \nmorning. Tonight should be the coldest, with lows in the mid 20s to \nmid 30s. High temperatures should gradually moderate through the \nweek, with near to above normal highs expected from Tue (low to mid \n60s) to Thu and Fri (mid 60s to low 70s).",
